==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|unusual|-ly|id2=adverbial}} or {{af|en|un-|usually|id1=negative}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʌnˈjuːʒuəli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-unusually.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|un|usu|al|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In an [[unusual]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|She's '''unusually''' happy for someone who's just broken her leg.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=David Langford|title=The Sex Column and Other Misprints|page=66
|passage=My convention diary is '''unusually''' disjointed, since I was mingily commuting from Berkshire rather than pay £65 per night for a single room.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|unwontedly}}

